WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.420
- Hi, I'm Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:03.213
And this is how I became Mysterio.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.370
When they pitched Mysterio to me,

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.880
they were like, he's
gonna be the new Avenger.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.120
He's gonna be one of the
new members of the MCU.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.500
And they needed a specific
type of actor I think

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.170
to be able to pull that off.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.040
And I just loved that.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.850
I mean, I love that, you
know, they need a particular

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.130
kind of skill set to play this part.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.120
Which was just exciting to me.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.200
And when Jon Watts
approached me about Mysterio,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.560
I thought, oh my god,
there's so many interesting

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.880
facets to him, and his
back story's really cool.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.290
And I do this thing whenever I'm looking

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.400
at a character where I'm always like

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.260
if they're one way,
I'm always wondering if

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.100
there's the opposite way to play it.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.700
Or if it's the opposite way,

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:47.960
I'm always looking for the other way.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.600
I think people tend to write things

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.710
or they tend to think of things very like,

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:52.940
oh this person's a good person,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.180
or this person's a bad person.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.960
I think we're much more complex than that,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.570
generally speaking.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:02.960
And I get so bored of
villains, or bad guys,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.510
or women in movies that are, you know,

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.730
they're mustache twirling
and they're just bad

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.870
'cause they want something.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.880
And they just have this sort
of, they want the money,

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.060
they want the power, blah, blah, blah.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.690
And it's become less interesting to me.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.220
So playing that in a world where

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.090
I think his logic makes a lot of sense.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.650
You know, he says something very clear,

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.850
regardless of the power that, you know,

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.970
should be bestowed, it
shouldn't be bestowed

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.990
on somebody who is not
mature enough to hold it.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.330
Because he knows the power of these things

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.150
that Tony has created.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.150
And the power of the MCU.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.330
And he respects it.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.650
I don't think there's a moment
where he doesn't respect it.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.770
And I just think he needs to make sure

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.110
all this work that he's done, with Tony,

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.260
is in the right hands.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.410
And that really is the
intention I had the entire time.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.840
And I don't think that's a bad intention.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.230
I think that's actually a really,

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.270
really, really good intention.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.330
It gets bad when he feels like, in order

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.490
to get that message across,
people need to get hurt.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:01.805
And that's that not very fine line,

00:02:01.805 --> 00:02:05.530
but that is the line that separates him.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.300
But his intention always has to be good.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.460
And I don't ever wanna
play a character who just,

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.163
is just bad, like is just
bad purely, you know.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.380
He always believes he's
doing the right thing.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.030
I mean the Quentin Beck, or you know,

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.660
the number of aliases that
he goes under in the comics,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.000
his intention always is basically envy.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.630
It's based on jealousy.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.300
But he uses this idea of illusion

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.320
and psychoanalysis, and all these sort of,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.310
all this knowledge he has
to manipulate situations.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.460
It's different because I think
his intention is actually

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.950
a better intention than
it ever is in the comics.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:43.270
And I don't think my Quentin
Beck, or my Mysterio,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.080
wants to really mess with Peter.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.300
I feel like he has to.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.380
And there is a distinct difference there.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.430
Because I think if you really get into it,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.730
a lot of times you see
characters like this

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.760
go, you know, oh, ha, ha,
ha, you shouldn't have

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.346
found yourself here Peter, you know.

00:02:57.346 --> 00:03:00.710
Oh, like I've told you so
many times never to walk

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.770
across this bridge and now
here you are, you know.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:05.320
And I was like, no, I
need to play a character

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.000
that tells him never to
walk across that bridge,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.630
and then he does, and he proves to me

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:14.380
that he's not mature enough
to wield all this power,

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.213
by walking across that bridge.

00:03:15.213 --> 00:03:18.070
And I say, man, I told you
not to walk across the bridge.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.440
Like I told you, almost like a parent.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:24.160
And now you are, and now we
have to do something about it.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.510
And that makes it just
so much more complex

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.140
for a lesson for Peter.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.730
Because as you grow up

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.870
the world becomes much more complicated.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.490
And I think that's what's
so cool about this movie,

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.960
is the world becomes so much
more complicated for Peter.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.400
- It's really nice to
have somebody to talk to

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.820
about superhero stuff, you know.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:42.760
- Anytime.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.650
The first scene I ever shot was the scene

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.500
where I enter and I
throw those green lasers

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.830
out of my hands, that you
don't want any part of this.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.860
I just was basically put on the suit,

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.420
thrown onset, and jumped off a platform,

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.590
and I was in the MCU.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.270
And, you know, that's overwhelming.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.160
And it took me about two months to like

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.280
even figure out what
the heck was going on.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.060
So, right when I finished, I felt like,

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.750
oh, I got it now, you know.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.990
Anybody who's searching for a new idea,

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.130
who never feels like any idea's bad,

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.330
that's what it feels
like to work with Marvel.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.540
And now they have, over these many years,

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.820
the funds to be able to
come up with any idea.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.630
When the best idea is there.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.410
And they take real risks.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.300
And to me, entertainment and all that,

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.730
but really art, is all about that.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.980
No matter what size it is,
rather it's like for pop culture,

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.270
or whether you're doing it for two people

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:28.900
who don't know, that's
what it's all about.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.380
That's the fun, that's the delight.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.310
They just, Marvel has not lost

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.640
their delight in the process.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.070
And I think that's why so many audiences

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.120
are delighted by the movies,
and keep coming back.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.080
You may not be ready, but
this is my responsibility.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.420
Well I think this movie's
really about making a movie.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:48.350
And I think I get to play
like director, and producer,

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:52.040
and writer, and actor,
all in one character.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.810
And I get to play good actor,
I get to play bad actor.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.160
And I don't think you ever
know where the performance is,

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.470
which is what I love about acting anyway.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:01.770
There's so many actors out there

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:04.080
talking about the importance
of the creative process,

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.440
which I think is really important.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.080
And I think it's actually
really beautiful.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.110
I mean I've devoted my life to it.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.640
But, at the same time, I
think it's totally absurd.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.360
And I think you have to have

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:15.970
a sense of humor about all of it.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:16.803
And what I love about Mysterio

00:05:16.803 --> 00:05:19.600
is he's just a comment on how amazing

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:24.400
and how kind of ridiculous
movies and movie making is.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.180
And what we will believe.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.550
And why we'll believe it.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.300
- [Interviewer] What part of the costume

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.830
made you most feel like Mysterio?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:36.000
- The pink leather g-string
that Mysterio wears

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.293
really makes me feel like the character.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.263
Ah no.

00:05:41.263 --> 00:05:43.380
It's the woolen cape that lights up.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.860
It's the hot battery pack on my back,

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:49.140
electrifying the disco ball
that is my chest plate.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.957
When I feel that burning
warmth on my lower backside,

00:05:53.957 --> 00:05:56.190
that's when I really
feel like the character.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.793
- [Interviewer] Think
we'll see Mysterio again?

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.980
- Ah, I don't know if that's up to me.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.253
I feel like that's up to Mysterio.

